{"id":"word:hebrew:H2945","type":"word","title":"טַף","subtitle":"H2945 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a family (mostly used collectively in the singular)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to טַף (H2945) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 42 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"טַף (ṭaph) means a family (mostly used collectively in the singular) First listed occurrence: 2Chr 20 13."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"טַף","transliteration":"ṭaph","pronunciation":"taf","strong":"H2945","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2945","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["טַפָּ/ם֙","וְ/הַ/טָּֽף","וְ/הַ/טַּ֔ף","טַפְּ/כֶ֑ם","טַפָּ֖/ם"],"morphs":[["HNcmsc/Sp3mp",6],["HC/Td/Ncmsa",6],["HTd/Ncmsa",5],["HNcmsc/Sp2mp",5],["HC/Ncmsc/Sp2mp",3],["HC/Ncmsa",3],["HNcmsc/Sp1cp",3],["HR/Ncmsc/Sp2mp",3],["HNcmsa",2],["HR/Ncmsa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"a family (mostly used collectively in the singular)","usage":"(little) children (ones), families.","full":"H2945. taph טַף 42 noun masculine collective children (as going with quick, tripping steps; Ethiopic Di 1251 ) — טַף Jer 41:16 11 t.; טָ֑ף 40:7 5 t.; suffix טַמֵּנוּ Gen 43:8 5 t.; טַמְּכֶם 45:19 10 t.; טַמָּם 34:29 6 t.; never construct and never plural (in 47:24 omitted by ᵐ5 , compare Di); — children, little ones , 34:29 (E) + 18 t. J E (Genesis Exodus Numbers), also Deut 1:39 8 t. D (including Josh 1:14 ; 8:35 ); P only Num 31:9 , 17 , 18 , where note בַּטָּ֑ף זָכָר 31:17 = young boys , and בַּנָּשִׁים הַטַף 31:18 = young girls ; also Judg 18:21 ; 21:10 ; 2Sam 15:22 ; Jer 40:7 ; 41:16 ; 43:6 ; Ezek 9:6 ; 2Chr 20:13 ; 31:18 ; Ezra 8:21 ; Est 3:13 ; 8:11 ; the words וְהַטָ֑ף וְנָשִׁים מְתִים Deut 2:34 ; 3:6 including all inhabitants; so וְהַטָּף וְהַנָּשִׁים אֲנָשִׁים 31:12 ; Jer 40:7 ; 43:6 ; טַף distinguished from וּבְּתוּלָה בָּחוּר Ezek 9:6 ; also from בְּנֵיהֶם 2Chr 20:13 , and from וּבְנוֺתֵיהֶם בְנֵיהֶם 31:18 . **Note that the word includes (or implies) women as well as children, in following: Gen 47:12 ; Exod 12:37 (E), 10:10 ; 10:24 (J), Num 32:16 ; 32:17 (J E; compare Di on 32:26 ).","rootNote":"from 2952 (perhaps referring to the tripping gait of children);","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"2Chr 20 13","keyReferences":["2Chr 20 13","2Chr 31 18","2Sam 15 22","Deut 1 39","Deut 2 34","Deut 3 6","Deut 3 19","Deut 20 14"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":42,"occurrences":[{"reference":"2Chr 20 13","book":"2Chr","chapter":20,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"טַפָּ֖/ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"2Chr 31 18","book":"2Chr","chapter":31,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"טַפָּ֧/ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"2Sam 15 22","book":"2Sam","chapter":15,"verse":22,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/טַּ֖ף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"Deut 1 39","book":"Deut","chapter":1,"verse":39,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/טַפְּ/כֶם֩","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmsc/Sp2mp"},{"reference":"Deut 2 34","book":"Deut","chapter":2,"verse":34,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/הַ/טָּ֑ף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Td/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"Deut 3 6","book":"Deut","chapter":3,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/הַ/טָּֽף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Td/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"Deut 3 19","book":"Deut","chapter":3,"verse":19,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/טַפְּ/כֶם֮","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmsc/Sp2mp"},{"reference":"Deut 20 14","book":"Deut","chapter":20,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/הַ/טַּ֨ף","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Td/Ncmsa"},{"reference":"Deut 29 10","book":"Deut","chapter":29,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"טַפְּ/כֶ֣ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc/Sp2mp"},{"reference":"Deut 31 12","book":"Deut","chapter":31,"verse":12,"engl